n they recorded, they were instrumental in infusing retro rock elements into what would eventually become the New Wave sound. \"Lo and Edmonds formed an on-again off-again band called Rockpile, named for Edmonds 1972 LP.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Angry Young Men Edition Part 1","url":"https://shows.acast.com/hit-parade/episodes/695d4f780c30a1408dc2baf3"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Shift to New Wave","body":"Around 1978, Dave Edmonds himself transitioned his musical direction towards New Wave. \"Dave Edmunds, too, had shifted in a new wavy direction.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Angry Young Men Edition Part 1","url":"https://shows.acast.com/hit-parade/episodes/695d4f780c30a1408dc2baf3"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":94287008083116,"type":"song","name":"I Hear You Knocking","work_year":1971,"list_id":176272515229071,"list":"UK nº1 · 1970s","src":"singles","rank":294,"year":1970,"note":"6 semanas","yt":"hMjwb13TFCo","scaruffi":null},{"id":94287008083116,"type":"song","name":"I Hear You Knocking","work_year":1971,"list_id":114443832640485,"list":"Billboard Year-End 1971","src":"singles","rank":81,"year":1971,"note":"","yt":"hMjwb13TFCo","scaruffi":null},{"id":94287008083116,"type":"song","name":"I Hear You Knocking","work_year":1971,"list_id":132335824845498,"list":"Billboard Year-End Hot 100","src":"charts","rank":81,"year":1971,"note":null,"yt":"hMjwb13TFCo","scaruffi":null},{"id":94287008083116,"type":"song","name":"I Hear You Knocking","work_year":1971,"list_id":167954413065108,"list":"UK Singles Chart","src":"charts","rank":10,"year":1971,"note":null,"yt":"hMjwb13TFCo","scaruffi":null},{"id":14570821165962,"type":"album","name":"Rockpile","list_id":240735758437916,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Rock & Roll","src":"musthear","rank":61,"year":1972,"note":null,"yt":"B6uPkumtEXg","scaruffi":null},{"id":1